Abstract = {The cytological study of the endosperm of T. corymbosa seed with the
   light microscope showed that its reserve is not mobilized during the 1st
   stages of germination. Its degradation begins 60 h after the radicle
   emerges, reaching its maximum within the following 60 h. The endosperm,
   formed by a hygroscopic polysaccharide, probably a galactomannan,
   evidently provides the necessary moisture for germination.},
